    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d138">

                <pb facs="0175" n="159" sameAs="frus:frus1947v08/pg159"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">561.333D3/9–1247: Airgram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Certain Diplomatic
                        Representatives in the American Republics </hi><anchor n="6"
                        xml:id="d138-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-09-12">September 12,
                        1947</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>On September 11, 1947, the Inter-American Coffee Board passed a motion
                    recommending the continuation of the Inter-American Coffee <pb facs="0176"
                        n="160" xml:id="pg160"/> Agreement for one year beginning October 1,
                        1947.<anchor n="7" xml:id="d138-f2"/> Protocol for continuation is the same
                    as Enclosure No. 3 to Instruction to United States Delegate to the
                    Inter-American Coffee Board<anchor n="8" xml:id="d138-f3"/> with minor changes.
                    Copies of this instruction were sent by transmittal slips in August to Embassies
                    receiving this airgram.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d138-f1" n="6" type="source" xml:id="d138-f1-content">
                <p>At Rio de Janeiro, Bogotá, Tegucigalpa, Mexico City, Guatemala, Caracas, Lima,
                    Habana, Port-au-Prince, San José Ciudad Trujillo, Managua, Quito, and San
                    Salvador.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d138-f2" n="7" xml:id="d138-f2-content">
                <p>Department of State Treaties and Other International Acts Series No. 1768; 62
                    Stat. (pt. 2) 1658.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d138-f3" n="8" xml:id="d138-f3-content">
                <p>Dated August 4, not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
